  "description": "DOGXAC crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a c d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H252 Dy12 Fe8 N32 O96,8(C2 H3 N1),6(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1O (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2O (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3O (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4O (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5O (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6O (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Fe1O (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2O (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3O (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe4O (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.379-3.745 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.54-111.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C142H300Dy12Fe8N40O102. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 tea (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 12 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
